{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function keepPreviousData<T>(previousData: T | undefined): T | undefined;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/utils.ts#L582","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/query-core/src/utils.ts:582"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Intended to be passed as a query's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"placeholderData"},{"type":"text","value":" option, for example\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"placeholderData: keepPreviousData"},{"type":"text","value":". Instead of resetting the query's data to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"},{"type":"text","value":" while a new\nquery key is fetching, it keeps displaying the previously fetched data until the new data arrives."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"t","children":[{"type":"text","value":"T"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"T"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"previousdata","children":[{"type":"text","value":"previousData"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"T"},{"type":"text","value":" | "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The data of the previous query key, passed by the observer."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"T"},{"type":"text","value":" | "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The previous data, unchanged."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"new QueryObserver(queryClient, {\n  queryKey: ['posts', page],\n  queryFn: () => fetchPosts(page),\n  placeholderData: keepPreviousData,\n})","lang":"ts"}],"headings":[{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"t","text":"T","level":3},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"previousdata","text":"previousData","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction keepPreviousData<T>(previousData: T | undefined): T | undefined;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/utils.ts:582](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/utils.ts#L582)\n\nIntended to be passed as a query's `placeholderData` option, for example\n`placeholderData: keepPreviousData`. Instead of resetting the query's data to `undefined` while a new\nquery key is fetching, it keeps displaying the previously fetched data until the new data arrives.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### T\n\n`T`\n\n## Parameters\n\n### previousData\n\n`T` \\| `undefined`\n\nThe data of the previous query key, passed by the observer.\n\n## Returns\n\n`T` \\| `undefined`\n\nThe previous data, unchanged.\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nnew QueryObserver(queryClient, {\n  queryKey: ['posts', page],\n  queryFn: () => fetchPosts(page),\n  placeholderData: keepPreviousData,\n})\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: keepPreviousData\ntitle: keepPreviousData\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction keepPreviousData<T>(previousData: T | undefined): T | undefined;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/utils.ts:582](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/utils.ts#L582)\n\nIntended to be passed as a query's `placeholderData` option, for example\n`placeholderData: keepPreviousData`. Instead of resetting the query's data to `undefined` while a new\nquery key is fetching, it keeps displaying the previously fetched data until the new data arrives.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### T\n\n`T`\n\n## Parameters\n\n### previousData\n\n`T` \\| `undefined`\n\nThe data of the previous query key, passed by the observer.\n\n## Returns\n\n`T` \\| `undefined`\n\nThe previous data, unchanged.\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nnew QueryObserver(queryClient, {\n  queryKey: ['posts', page],\n  queryFn: () => fetchPosts(page),\n  placeholderData: keepPreviousData,\n})\n```\n"}
